 inspired by famous animal characters in literature.\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-06-04\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-07-06\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"BestAnimalNames Editorial Team\",\"url\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/about/\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"BestAnimalNames\",\"url\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com\"},\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/literary-animal-names-books/\"},\"wordCount\":2275,\"articleBody\":\"📋 Table of Contents  🐾 Introduction Names inspired by famous animal characters in literature. Whether you're naming a new pet, a character in your story, or just exploring for fun, you've come to the right place. At Animal Name Generator, we've curated thousands of name ideas across hundreds of animal species to help you find that perfect match. Our database spans {oriental-shorthair}, {bumblebee-bat}, {pixie-bob}, {yellow-warbler}, {sea-lion}, {blue-tit}, and many more — each with 160+ hand-picked names. This guide focuses on bringing you the best of the best in one convenient place. 📛 The Complete List — 100 Literary Animal Names 1–10 <strong>Obi-Wan Kenobi</strong> — This playful name is perfect for a pet with a big personality and a love for attention. <strong>Furricane</strong> — Inspired by pop culture, this name works great for pets that have a dramatic flair or star quality. <strong>Sir Barksalot</strong> — A clever twist that suits a smart and mischievous companion who always keeps you laughing. <strong>Luke Skybarker</strong> — This name captures the essence of a loyal and loving friend who brightens every day. <strong>Bilbo Waggins</strong> — With a name like this, your pet is sure to be the talk of the dog park — in the best way possible. <strong>Pablo Escobark</strong> — A unique choice that reflects your pet's one-of-a-kind personality and charm. <strong>Chairman Meow</strong> — Inspired by pop culture, this name works great for pets that have